.nh
.TH "PB-RECORDINGS-STOP" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-recordings-stop - Stop the recording of the terminal session you are attached to


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb recordings stop [session-id] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Stop recording the terminal session that a pb connect on this computer is attached to. The
session ID is optional; name it when you are attached to more than one session. A recording a
rule started can only be stopped by an admin.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for stop

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb recordings stop
  pb recordings stop S123 --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-recordings(1)\fP
